---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About Us">
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="title_image">
      <p><img src="/pictures/urbanism-club-logo.png" alt="Title of the website: Urbanism Club" /></p>
    </div>
    <div class="tagline">
      <p>University of Cincinnati <a href="https://www.uc.edu/campus-life/csi.html">Registered Student Organization</a></p>
      <p>Student chapter of the <a href="https://planning.org">American Planning Association</a> (Planning Student Organization)</p>
      <p>UC Urbanism <a href="https://strongtowns.org">Strong Towns</a> Local Conversation</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="image">
      <p><img src="/pictures/urbanism-club-group.png" alt="Urbanism Club Group" /></p>
    </div>
    <div class="lines">
      <p>Urbanism Club aims to connect students and other members of the Uptown community; through </p>
      <p>discussions with local experts and others in the know; sharing new projects and ideas; and group</p>
      <p>projects and activities. Host to the University of Cincinnati student chapter of the American Planning </p>
      <p>Association(APA) (Planning Student Organization(PSO)), and the UC Urbanism Strong Towns Local </p>
      <p>Conversation, we support UC DAAP planning students, and embody Strong Towns principles.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main class="site">
    <h2>About us</h2>
    <p>Urbanism Club is a student-led, community organization that aims to connect students and other members of the Uptown community who are interested in urbanism. </p>
    <p>Our members learn about and advocate for better communities through: discussions with local experts and community organizations, projects focused on regional issues, volunteer opportunities, workshops, and more.</p>

    <figure><img src="/media/group-park.jpg" alt="" /></figure>

    <h2>What is Urbanism?</h2>
    <p>Urbanism refers to the way of life or characteristics or a city or town. We think of it as “being of the city,” an active participant in your locality.</p>

    <figure><img src="/media/campus-walk.jpg" alt="" /></figure>

    <h2>Our Main Goals</h2>
    <div class="goals">
      <div>
        <h3>Educate</h3>
        <p>Provide opportunities to learn more about urban challenges, initiatives, organizations, and more from the area and beyond. </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Connect</h3>
        <p>Create a space for individuals interested in urbanism to connect with each other, local experts, community organizers, and more. </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Advocate</h3>
        <p>Support local initiatives and organizations by volunteering, campaigning, and sharing resources.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure><img src="/media/club-meeting.jpg" alt="" /></figure>

    <h2>Affiliate Organizations</h2>
    <p>Urbanism Club is home to the University of Cincinnati Planning Student Organization, officially registered with the American Planning Organization. Additionally, we are an official local StrongTowns Conversation, alongside friend of the club Civic Cincinnati, and an All Aboard Ohio Affiliate Club. </p>
    <div class="logo-row">
      <img src="/media/pso.png" alt="" />
      <img src="/media/apa.png" alt="" />
      <img src="/media/strong-towns.svg" alt="" />
      <img src="/media/all-aboard-ohio.png" alt="" />
    </div>
    <p>To get more information on any of these organizations, check out our Resources page!</p>

    <h2>Leadership Team</h2>
    <div class="lines">
      <p>President and Treasurer, <a href="https://www.fenleyjones.com">Fenley Jones</a></p>
      <p>Engagement Coordinator, Matthew Sayers</p>
      <p>Education Coordinator, Michael Uhlemann</p>
      <p>Advocacy Coordinator, AJ Domelle</p>
      <p>Advocacy Coordinator, James McDermott</p>
      <p>APA (PSO) Chair, Henry Bogzevitz</p>
      <p>Strong Towns Chair, Michael Uhlemann</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
